title: 'Cid Debrief: Theoretical team analysis (no code): "How does Warpline let AI agents work acros'
summary: 'Theoretical team analysis (no code): "How does Warpline let AI agents work across many branches at once?" A 5-lens panel (Arky/architect, Loid/forge, Cid/captain, Aegis/security, Jinx/advocate) converged on: Warpline turns git''s O(branches) serial human-gated merge into O(genuine-meaning-collisions) parallel forecast + one CONSOLIDATE; the long-lived branch is likely the wrong atom for swarms (agents emit immutable content-addressed PICKs into a shared continuously-forecast fabric; keep a PICK-group/weft atomic transaction + an ephemeral scratch view). HONEST SCOPE: step-change for FAN-OUT swarms (disjoint symbols), neutral for DEEP-OVERLAP (one hot symbol); the headline win is agreement-visibility + cross-branch semantic-break detection, NOT magic convergence (a Merkle-closure rounding error in practice). STRATEGIC KICKER: Jinx''s cathedral-vs-linter objection confirms the companion-first GTM — ship the built read-only Oracle as a semantic CI gate on git worktrees (= Warpline Guard) NOW; build the fabric/replacement behind it by gravity. RANKED FOLLOW-UPS: (1) fix absorb worktree concurrency T-2026-06-23-003 via git-archive materialization + interim per-repo mutex (the literal gate to any parallel demo; Cid''s key finding: parsers need a real dir, NOT a git worktree); (2) build the N≥3-agents-on-the-SAME-feature consolidate fixture (prove < git-merge human labor, not the easy non-intersecting demo); (3) confront GAP-1 for the agent workload (config/tests/fixtures/prose = byte-merge fallback = the conflict-dense center of mass — the undesigned load-bearing wall); (4) close the Tier-0 invariant-conflict foot-gun (disjoint-but-jointly-wrong auto-weaves) + harden the weft-prose prompt-injection channel into reviewing agents (Aegis, highest severity); (5) design admission concurrency (per-domain optimistic CAS = generalize the merge-queue re-predict) + the cold-start trust ladder for fresh agent swarms. Converged confidence: architecture ~0.8 sound, product ~0.5 unproven until the write path runs and the same-feature contention fixture exists.'
